<Layout description="Explore reading options, keyboard controls, on-screen input, printable alternatives, and accessibility limitations at Large Print Crosswords." title="Accessibility — Large Print Crosswords"><div class="container prose"><header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">MADE TO FEEL WELCOMING</p><h1>Comfort comes first.</h1></header><p>We aim to make crosswords easier to read and operate. We use scalable text, high-contrast colors, visible keyboard focus, and clear labels. You can zoom using your browser without a restriction set by the site.</p><h2>Keyboard play</h2><p>Tab enters the crossword at its selected square. Use arrow keys within the board, Enter to change direction at a crossing, and Backspace to erase. Tab again leaves the board for the game controls. Clue buttons can also be reached using Tab.</p><h2>Helpful choices</h2><p>The game offers a Larger clues button. Sound is optional and starts off. Check results use text and underlines as well as color, and status messages are announced to assistive technology.</p><h2>Alternatives and limits</h2><p>A crossword is a spatial activity, and experiences with screen readers and voice input may vary. Each puzzle also includes text clues, a collapsible answer list, and a printable version. These features are accessibility measures, not a claim of complete WCAG conformance or legal certification.</p><a class="button button-outline" href="/how-to-play/">Read the playing guide</a></div></Layout>
